From 230449c82cf53438cb7c2d0420e28d7c466fe5a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:23:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add reproducible reviewed C++ AST conversion tool

Track the ast-grep-py 0.51.0 engine requirement, converter, tests and explicit
semantic rules before their first consumer. Syntax parsing handles C++ argument
boundaries, including nested template and lambda expressions. A literal-only
printf parser checks formats; independent checks reject severity/category or
message-skeleton changes. Unsupported rendering remains legacy and appears in
the inventory. Domain semantics and field types are explicitly reviewed, not
guessed from inline key=value labels.

Dry run prints a diff plus accepted/rejected inventory without source mutation;
all files validate before any writes. Exact reviewed-input fingerprints and
expected counts reject drift; repeated application makes no edits. Non-call
registry/include/assertion/formatting adjustments are separately recorded.
Consumer commits must include exact commands, tool versions, script/rule hashes,
input scope, prerequisite revision and adjustments. Earlier conversions are not
retroactively labeled as consumers of this tool.

Validation: ten tool-test methods, including all catalog mappings; six complete
before/after fixtures reproduce 84 planned call conversions exactly; dry-run
purity and second-run idempotence pass in each. Validator caught and corrected
uncommitted draft NET and LEVELDB category changes before application. No daemon
source changes in this prerequisite; no new full daemon suite claimed here.

(cherry picked from commit 43d5848cf66d39fa34b84890f59d2fad087f3615)

N3-Source-Commit: 43d5848cf66d39fa34b84890f59d2fad087f3615
N3-Source-Export: 0051

Canonical RPC catalog adaptation: the shared engine retains both synchronous and coroutine HTTP processors. Require count2 for their four identical reviewed authentication/whitelist diagnostics; retain exact-count drift rejection and every existing mapping/type/level/message invariant. This is a catalog scope adaptation, not a changed converter or weakened validation.

Coordinator integration provenance (canonical283 to ordered301):
The scripted commands, tool/rule hashes and historical validation receipts above are original-author provenance for the authored parent. They were not rerun on this composed parent and do not claim byte-for-byte regeneration or validation of it.
Application: git am -3 --keep-cr --keep-non-patch of the exact sealed original mailbox; no new conversion rollout.
Fold original0057 (719d747a2293bd9fdadc30ae8e05b01ea8639fce) and0060 (b6e0657d2091f128323dafa551b46d8248d7cad5) into their original AST-tool owner; existing sqlite-lifecycle.json is present here. Remove exactly storage-lifecycle-dbwrapper-1/2/3 catalog rules already obsolete under the shared MDBX owner; retain canonical RPC catalog count2. Method: original mailboxes applied with git am -3 --keep-cr --keep-non-patch; three obsolete JSON rule objects removed, no new conversion generated.
Composed compile/runtime: pending; no suites or benchmarks run during integration.

Coordinator ordered integration (2026-10-20):
Existing causal fixes and mechanical namespace/format adaptations are folded at their first responsible owner. Exact inputs and prefix adaptations are recorded in integration-next final delivery; original author provenance is retained.

